From: aiden build <build@aiden.local>
Subject: [PATCH] node: skip auxv secure-exec probe when header is absent

src/node_main.cc includes <sys/auxv.h> and calls getauxval(AT_SECURE) for
all Linux builds. The Luckfox Buildroot target uses a uClibc toolchain whose
sysroot does not provide sys/auxv.h, so the target Node.js 16.20.0 build
fails with:

  src/node_main.cc:92:10: fatal error: sys/auxv.h: No such file or directory

Use the auxv secure-exec probe only when the header is available. On targets
without the header, linux_at_secure keeps its existing false default and
Node.js still falls back to the uid/gid mismatch checks in SafeGetenv().

Aiden-local patch.
---
--- a/src/node_main.cc
+++ b/src/node_main.cc
@@ -89,7 +89,15 @@
 #else
 // UNIX
 #ifdef __linux__
+#if defined(__has_include)
+#if __has_include(<sys/auxv.h>)
 #include <sys/auxv.h>
+#define NODE_HAVE_GETAUXVAL 1
+#endif
+#elif !defined(__UCLIBC__)
+#include <sys/auxv.h>
+#define NODE_HAVE_GETAUXVAL 1
+#endif
 #endif  // __linux__
 #if defined(__POSIX__) && defined(NODE_SHARED_MODE)
 #include <string.h>
@@ -117,7 +125,7 @@
   }
 #endif
 
-#if defined(__linux__)
+#if defined(NODE_HAVE_GETAUXVAL)
   node::per_process::linux_at_secure = getauxval(AT_SECURE);
 #endif
   // Disable stdio buffering, it interacts poorly with printf()
